<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Continental Congress</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1775">1775</a>–<a href="/years/1781">1781</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/continental-congress">Continental Congress</a> was the assembly of delegates from the thirteen American colonies that met from May 1775, after fighting had begun at Lexington and Concord. It created the Continental Army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-washington">George Washington</a>, adopted the Declaration of Independence on 4 July 1776 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/articles-of-confederation">Articles of Confederation</a>, and governed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> until 1781, when it became the Congress of the Confederation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-continental-congress.jpg" alt="Second Continental Congress" width="320" height="233" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Robert Edge Pine / Edward Savage · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Congress_voting_independence.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
